# Anthiel agent conventions

## Tooling

- Package manager: **Bun** (`bun install`, `bun run <script>`, `bunx`)
- Lint: `bun run lint` (oxlint). Format: `bun run format` (oxfmt).
- Typecheck: `bun run typecheck` from root or per app.
- Project map: consumer repo `AGENTS.md` when present.

## Code changes

- Minimize scope — smallest correct diff; do not change unrelated code.
- Match existing conventions in the file and feature you touch.
- Named exports; function declarations for components (`function Foo()`).
- Use `type` for type-only exports.
- Comments only for non-obvious business logic — not on every line.

## Git

- **Do not commit** unless the user explicitly asks.
- **Do not push** unless the user explicitly asks.
- No force push to main, no `--no-verify`, no amending pushed commits.

## Stack skills

Deep workflows live in installed Anthiel skills (load on demand):

| Area | Skill |
| --- | --- |
| Frontend / backoffice | `anthiel-frontend` |
| Backend | `anthiel-backend` |
| Desktop POS | `anthiel-desktop` |
| Tracked multi-step work | `anthiel-task-boards` |

Companion rules: `anthiel-frontend.mdc`, `anthiel-backend.mdc`, `anthiel-desktop.mdc`, `anthiel-task-boards.mdc`, `anthiel-bun.mdc`, `anthiel-copy.mdc`.
